WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.960
Before he was swole

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.420
Before he was existentially depressed

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.220
and before he was a cartoon

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.480
"Never leave the cave without it"

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.620
He was a swole existentially depressed literal cartoon in

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.740
Batman the Animated Series

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:32.220
Return to a time when pop culture wasn't oversaturated with superheroes,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.160
"They sell t-shirts of me. I've become a cliché."

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.860
Animation still ruled after school and dial-up internet gave us a few precious minutes offline

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:55.380
*boopy beepy noises*

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.940
And spend some time with Kevin Conroy's iconic Bruce Wayne

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.580
An industrialist with the money of Tony Stark

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.780
and the fashion sense of Dwight Schrute

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.840
But when night falls, this punch-a-holic will become the Batman,

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.760
the world's greatest detective

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.700
who's also the world's greatest ninja

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.620
greatest hacker,

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.980
"I've accessed Gotham's electrical mainframe."

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:19.019
"There's another computer uplink to this one"

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.760
"I'm tracing the link now"

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:21.920
greatest magician

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.140
"You've got the makings of a great magician"

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.300
and the greatest... ventriloquist?

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.500
"When I studied with Zatara The Magician, he taught me about ventriloquism."

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.980
Wow, this Batman does a lot.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.040
But does he... dance?

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.400
But this cape isn't crusading solo.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.500
He has a whole cave full of allies

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.320
Like

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:55.820
Alfred Pennyworth, Butler of Batman, but king of sick burns.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:57.820
"Clayface is losing his integrity"

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.800
"I wasn't aware he ever had any to begin with."

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.960
Ohhhhhhhh!

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.420
Robin, the Boy Wonder. As in, boy I wonder what screwed him up between this show and Titans.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.060
"YAHOOO!""

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.180
"F*** Batman."

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:15.320
Batgirl, a college kid whose relationship with Bats is super creepy after seeing The Killing Joke movie.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.640
"Barbara, come in"

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.820
"You've grown"

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.000
Ewwwwwuyh!

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:25.700
And Commissioner Gordon, a humble civil servant tormented by a billionaire psychopath determined to drive him insane

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:26.720
"Batman!"

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.560
"Busy night?"

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:28.060
*gasp*

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.740
"Helen, get me-" *gasp*

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:30.840
"We need to talk"

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:32.400
*gasp*

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.540
"Nigma's making a comeback."

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.400
Come on, give him a break, Bats.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.720
We all know you're a ninja, you don't have to keep proving it to Grandpa Cop, alright?

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:44.680
jeezzz

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.400
Together, they'll protect Gotham.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.760
A city trapped somewhere between 1932 and 1992

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:57.080
A town where the crime is up, the nights are long, and the people are rectangles

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:01.200
It's a city under siege for the best rogues gallery in animation history

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.720
Featuring character defining portrayals of Two-Face.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.260
"You're talkin' to the wrong Harvey."

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.400
Mr. Freeze.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:15.560
"To never again walk on a summer's day with a hot wind in your face. And a warm hand to hold."

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.540
Harley Quinn.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.660
"Harley Quinn, pleased to meetcha."

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.400
The best Joker ever.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.560
Yeah, I said it.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.260
And a bat menageries worth of animals

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.620
Jeez Batman. Maybe you should stick to something less threatening? Like a penguin.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.680
"Now, Roberta!"

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.240
"Nice shot."

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:51.860
"We did it!"

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.440
So light up the bat-signal, and revisit the highs

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.200
"I am vengeance."

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.140
"I am the night!"

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.480
"I am Batman!"

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:03.780
And the lows.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.560
"You've made her a monster!"

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.580
"I believe she would disagree."

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.420
of the darkest adaptation of Batman ever made.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:11.860
Literally the darkest

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.560
because they drew it on black paper

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.160
that wasn't afraid to hit kids with complex philosophy

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:20.860
"Santayana says that those who forget the past are condemned to repeat it."

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.520
Then break it up with a guy kicking a werewolf in the face

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.080
"If it's a fight you're looking for, try starting one with me!"

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.540
See DC, that's all we want.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:34.020
A definitive portrait of a beloved character that balances multiple tones across dozens of hours

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:38.480
that can only happen with a perfect creative team and lands at the perfect time in the cultural zeitgeist.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.780
Is that so hard?

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.380
"Listen up scum wad."

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:47.340
"Here's how it works, slimeball."

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:49.140
"Alright scum bucket."

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.860
"Too late dirtbag."

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.300
"What do you want?"

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.320
"Has Professor Crane lost his appetite?"

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:57.660
*startled noise*

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:58.800
"Who's back there?"

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.100
"You..."

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:39.580
"Gas attack!"

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.240
"Hey!"

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.820
"Stop shooting, you lunatic!"

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.500
"We're sitting on a powder keg!"

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.340
And Batmanthumbsup.gif

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:17.680
Nope, the other one.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:19.820
That's the one!

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.720
Okay, we need to talk about the intro for a sec

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:35.560
Has anyone else noticed that the crooks are just two guys who happen to be walking past the bank at night?

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.880
Then when the entrance explodes, they run away like any sane person would do?

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.420
They don't even have any loot on 'em!

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.240
Sure, fine, they pull guns on Batman.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.980
But for all they know, he's the psycho going around blowing up banks!

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.340
And Batman doesn't know who did it either, he had to drive there!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.360
But does that stop him from beating the crap out of 'em and leavin' 'em for the cops?

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:52.100
Without any evidence to convict 'em on?

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.200
This is vigilantes are a bad idea, you guys.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:13.260
*reads comments*

